actual.value:
The global Corona virus pandemic has resulted in the following changes for this project:

1. All trainings were scheduled to take place in 2019, with 2020 being the roll-out to other locations. In 2019 we managed to do training 1 (leadership with the board) and will do a combined training on Basics of Hydraulics and NRW (scheduled in December). The reason for this are the restrictions in public gatherings (including trainings) imposed by Zambian National government. The postponed trainings are scheduled for the first half of 2020, leaving the role-out of trainings to the second part of 2020. A key challenge is that proposed Dutch Experts are unable to travel. As a mitigating factor we will change some classroom trainings to digital trainings and will have to utilize more staff that is present in Zambia. Wit the offered 3 months extension we expect that the vast majority (>90%) of the proposed training activities can be conducted before 31-12-2021;

2. Our hardware procurements are slightly delayed due to travel restrictions: where we planned to bring hardware in with visitors / trainers, hardware now has to be transported by couriers (attracting additional fees);

3. The Zambian economy (and local currency) is hit hard. The financial position of the water companies is very much affected by this. The proposed own contributions of LgWSC are uncertain (particularly for the proposed 25.000 euro for the best business case)
